@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`Coupons.use` records the id of the order that used a single-use coupon, and `Coupons.giveBack(code, order)` releases it only when that order is the recorded one. `OrderService.cancel` in `src/orders.ts` calls `giveBack(order.coupon, order.customer)`, passing the customer name instead of the order id, so the release never matches. See proposal.md.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** cancellation releases the coupon as the README states.
+
+**Non-Goals:** shipping rules (already correct), changes to `Coupons`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Pass `id` to `giveBack` in `cancel`. `Coupons` already has the right ownership check, so the fix stays at the call site.
