+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+A customer cancelled an order that used a single-use welcome code, and the code was then refused as already used on the corrected order. The README says a cancelled order gives its single-use coupon back.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Cancelling an order gives back its single-use coupon, so the same code can be used on a new order.
+- Out of scope: free shipping at exactly €50.00. Support reported a €4.90 charge on goods of exactly fifty euros, but the current code and the `order-pricing` spec already make that shipping free (an earlier change fixed it; `npm test` covers 4999 and 5000). If the report came from an order priced before that fix it needs no code change; if goods were €50.00 before a discount and below it after, the charge is correct under the README ("after every discount"). No change is made for it.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `order-discounts`: adds the single-use coupon requirement (used once, returned on cancellation).
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/orders.ts` (`cancel`); tests under `test/`. No API changes.
